PairKey independently modifies the downloaded research copy, without any
involvement by Silence Laboratories:
- Adds a restricted, typed 2-of-2 constructor with local secret/public and
  weighted aggregate checks. This does not validate the interactive ceremony.
- Corrects duplicate party-ID validation to compare package IDs rather than
  complete (participant index, package ID) tuples.
- Preserves migration protocol errors when best-effort abort delivery fails;
  the research relay reports the transport failure separately.

- Adds an explicit research feature and a migration PPRF-proof corruption fixture
  gated behind it; disabled in default builds.

Modifications were made on 2026-10-10. Exact modifications are maintained in
patch-source.py and patches/research-keyshare.rs. Signing arithmetic is unchanged.
Original source notices are retained in the downloaded source and dependencies.
